      "body": "## Motivation\n\nFollow-up to #47387: broaden the numerical parity inputs of the balanced paged decode indexer test, as suggested in its review.\n\n## Modifications\n\nAdd `test_fp4_paged_logits_balanced_matches_per_row_random`. Inputs: Gaussian queries and head weights, random FP4 payload bytes covering every e2m1 code, e8m0 exponents mostly in the typical range plus ~1% at the extremes (0, 1, 126-128, 200, 254), shuffled pages, and ragged lengths including 0, 1, tile edges and past `max_len`. It runs 3 seeds × 32 / 64 heads × (ratio 1, ratio 2 with a candidate mask), and the balanced kernel must match the per-row kernel bit for bit.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nTest-only change. All 12 cases pass on H200. Each case compares ~340K visible scores, with thousands of distinct finite values and some infinities from the extreme scales.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nN/A (test-only).\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:white_check_mark: [Run #41175549856](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41175549856)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41175549838](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41175549838)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:white_check_mark: [Run #41175549854](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41175549854)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
